00:36:14,395 --> 00:36:16,436
[SPEAKER_02]: You just keep taking it further.

362
00:36:16,756 --> 00:36:24,000
[SPEAKER_02]: If you see, okay, factually, I cannot see anything more to be done in my virtue, and yet I still don't have the right view, well, then you go to the next step.

363
00:36:24,020 --> 00:36:34,906
[SPEAKER_02]: You just keep building it up until it's enough for you to be withdrawn, as that simile of the wet sticks would say.

364
00:36:37,908 --> 00:36:40,831
[SPEAKER_02]: You won't be able to light the fire until the sticks are dry.

365
00:36:41,431 --> 00:36:50,558
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you keep going further in these ways of drying up the sticks and until eventually it's dry enough for it to light up.

366
00:36:51,519 --> 00:36:56,002
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't have a way to predict how much is going to be necessary.

