00:42:16,631 --> 00:42:24,454
[SPEAKER_02]: Having felt touch with the body, he doesn't attend to the signs and features that would give rise to longing and upset.

409
00:42:24,474 --> 00:42:38,099
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if you are attending to your bodily sensations more for the purpose of giving rise to pleasure, which is what many people would conceive of as meditation, for example, then you're grasping signs and features.

410
00:42:39,379 --> 00:42:43,781
[SPEAKER_02]: So, yeah, that's why it goes in that order.

411
00:42:47,582 --> 00:42:56,705
[SPEAKER_00]: That's interesting, like, in the kind of, like, most of the contemporary set-up that we have in the West, of, like, meditation retreat, and even, like, monastery, and things like that.

412
00:42:57,525 --> 00:43:01,207
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, this whole gradual training is, like, taken totally the other way around.

