00:54:02,882 --> 00:54:04,444
[SPEAKER_02]: You just don't eat it for the wrong reason.

505
00:54:06,036 --> 00:54:19,961
[SPEAKER_02]: Sleepiness, clearing your mind from obstructive states and vigilance, you don't... yeah, you don't prevent even the obstructive states from arising.

506
00:54:20,902 --> 00:54:22,342
[SPEAKER_02]: You clear your mind from them.

507
00:54:23,143 --> 00:54:31,846
[SPEAKER_02]: So, like, as the suttas would say, once... like, how can you be passionate

508
00:54:35,226 --> 00:54:39,668
[SPEAKER_02]: How can it be passion, if you're dispassionate in regard to it?

509
00:54:41,288 --> 00:54:51,232
[SPEAKER_02]: As it would say, knowing a mind of passion is mind of passion, in the Satipaṭṭhāna Sutta, he would abide with the mind disengaged, independent from anything in the world.

510
00:54:51,512 --> 00:54:53,653
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you basically...

511
00:54:54,522 --> 00:55:07,470
[SPEAKER_02]: Even now, on that more intimate or personal level, you're learning how to not get engaged or involved with these things, even while they're there.

512
00:55:08,331 --> 00:55:10,993
[SPEAKER_02]: Same for the recollection and awareness.

513
00:55:11,013 --> 00:55:14,315
[SPEAKER_02]: That's already on that acute level of samādhi.

514
00:55:15,697 --> 00:55:19,421
[SPEAKER_02]: You wouldn't give in to even the tiniest actions.

515
00:55:20,362 --> 00:55:21,763
[SPEAKER_02]: The state is in your mind.

516
00:55:22,003 --> 00:55:23,325
[SPEAKER_02]: The pressure is there in your mind.

517
00:55:23,345 --> 00:55:30,131
[SPEAKER_02]: You haven't gotten rid of it, but you're not allowing even these tiniest actions to be motivated by it, which would result in

518
00:55:31,188 --> 00:55:32,329
[SPEAKER_02]: Reintroducing the craving.

519
00:55:33,349 --> 00:55:34,530
[SPEAKER_02]: And finally, the hindrances.

520
00:55:35,230 --> 00:55:40,032
[SPEAKER_02]: Again, you don't prevent things from being attractive or beautiful or pleasant.

521
00:55:40,092 --> 00:55:41,913
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't prevent them from being disagreeable.

522
00:55:42,713 --> 00:55:44,454
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't prevent tiredness from arising.

523
00:55:44,494 --> 00:55:47,936
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't prevent your mind from moving here and there.

524
00:55:47,976 --> 00:55:53,338
[SPEAKER_02]: And you don't prevent... You don't try to find the answer for everything, so as to not have doubt.

525
00:55:53,499 --> 00:55:56,980
[SPEAKER_02]: You just learn how to not be moved by those things.

526
00:55:57,040 --> 00:56:00,062
[SPEAKER_02]: And that that is like the culmination or the real

527
00:56:03,685 --> 00:56:12,673
[SPEAKER_02]: The core of the middle way, the most acute form of it, would be that.

528
00:56:12,894 --> 00:56:16,197
[SPEAKER_02]: That's why, actually, the sutta, that's the training.

529
00:56:16,677 --> 00:56:17,018
[SPEAKER_02]: That's it.

530
00:56:17,078 --> 00:56:19,700
[SPEAKER_02]: There's nothing after that.

531
00:56:20,201 --> 00:56:21,282
[SPEAKER_02]: If you just stick to this,

532
00:56:22,640 --> 00:56:23,821
[SPEAKER_02]: Eventually, you become an Arhat.

533
00:56:24,701 --> 00:56:34,768
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it doesn't talk about view and purification of understanding, because these things would... that would come as a result of you

534
00:56:35,709 --> 00:56:37,350
[SPEAKER_02]: Clearing your mind from these obstructions.

535
00:56:37,790 --> 00:56:56,877
[SPEAKER_02]: Obviously, to some extent, you need to get your right instruction and replace wrong views with right views, but it won't become wisdom until you are doing this, which is clearing the mind from these pollutions, like the dust in your eyes, as the suttas would call it.

536
00:56:57,117 --> 00:56:59,678
[SPEAKER_02]: Clearing the dust in your eyes, so that you would see what's already there.

537
00:57:00,638 --> 00:57:04,920
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's the... that's why, always in the suttas, with the four jhāna, like

538
00:57:06,093 --> 00:57:16,819
